"022:001 And David said, This is the house of the Lord God, and this is the altar for whole burnt offering for Israel.",
"022:002 And David gave orders to gather all the strangers that were in the land of Israel; and he appointed stone-hewers to hew polished stones to build the house to God.",
"022:003 And David prepared much iron for the nails of the doors and the gate; the hinges also and brass in abundance, there was no weighing of it.",
"022:004 And cedar threes without number: for the Sidonians and the Tyrians brought cedar trees in abundance to David.",
"022:005 And David said, My son Solomon is a tender child, and the house for me to build to the Lord is for superior magnificence for a name and for a glory through all the earth: I will make preparation for it. And David prepared abundantly before his death.",
"022:006 And he called Solomon his son, and commanded him to build the house for the Lord God of Israel.",
"022:007 And David said to Solomon, My child, it was in my heart to build a house to the name of the Lord God.",
"022:008 But the word of the Lord came to me, saying, You have shed blood abundantly, and have carried on great wars: you shall not build a house to my name, because you have shed much blood upon the earth before me.",
"022:009 Behold, a son shall be born to you, he shall be a man of rest; and I will give him rest from all his enemies round about: for his name shall be Solomon, and I will give peace and quietness to Israel in his days.",
"022:010 He shall build a house to my name; and he shall be a son to me, and I will be a father to him; and I will establish the throne of his kingdom in Israel for ever.",
"022:011 And now, my son, the Lord shall be with you, and prosper you; and you shall build a house to the Lord your God, as he spoke concerning you.",
"022:012 Only may the Lord give you wisdom and prudence, and strengthen you over Israel, both to keep and to do the law of the Lord your God.",
"022:013 Then will he prosper you, if you take heed to do the commandments and judgements which the Lord commanded Moses for Israel: be courageous and strong; fear not, nor be terrified.",
"022:014 And, behold, I according to my poverty have prepared for the house of the Lord one hundred thousand talents of gold, and a million talents of silver, and brass and iron without measure; for it is abundant; and I have prepared timber and stones; and do you add to these.",
"022:015 And of them that are with you do you add to the multitude of workmen; let there be artificers and masons, and carpenters, and every skilful workman in every work;",
"022:016 in gold and silver, brass and iron, of which there is no number. Arise and do, and the Lord be with you.",
"022:017 And David charged all the chief men of Israel to help Solomon his son, saying,",
"022:018 Is not the Lord with you? and he has given you rest round about, for he has given into your hands the inhabitants of the land; and the land is subdued before the Lord, and before his people.",
"022:019 Now set your hearts and souls to seek after the Lord your God: and rise, and build a sanctuary to your God to carry in the ark of the covenant of the Lord, and the holy vessels of God, into the house that is to be built to the name of the Lord."
